  "date": "2026-11-23",
  "category": "finance",
  "title_zh": "三家交易所降低借钱买股票的保证金比例，最低80%",
  "title_en": "Three stock exchanges lower the margin ratio for buying shares with borrowed money — minimum now 80%",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "zh": "11月22日，上海、深圳和北京三家证券交易所发布通知：经过中国证监会同意，投资者用融资的方式买股票时，最低保证金比例从100%降低到80%。新的规定从11月30日开始实行。",
      "en": "On November 22, the Shanghai, Shenzhen and Beijing stock exchanges issued a notice: with the approval of the China Securities Regulatory Commission (CSRC), when investors buy shares through margin financing, the minimum margin ratio will be lowered from 100% to 80%. The new rule takes effect on November 30."
    },
    {
      "zh": "这里的“融资”，就是投资者向证券公司借钱买股票。保证金比例越低，同样多的保证金就能借到越多的钱。比如，投资者有100万元保证金，以前最多能借100万元；11月30日以后，最多能借125万元。",
      "en": "\"Margin financing\" here means investors borrowing money from a securities company to buy shares. The lower the margin ratio, the more money the same amount of margin can borrow. For example, an investor with 1 million yuan of margin could borrow at most 1 million yuan before; after November 30, they can borrow up to 1.25 million yuan."
    },
    {
      "zh": "这个比例以前也调整过几次：2015年11月从50%提高到100%，2023年8月降低到80%，今年1月又提高到100%。监管部门表示，最近用融资买股票的交易明显减少了，市场的杠杆水平也不高。",
      "en": "This ratio has been adjusted several times before: in November 2015 it was raised from 50% to 100%, in August 2023 it was lowered to 80%, and in January this year it was raised to 100% again. The regulator said that trading in shares bought with borrowed money has clearly decreased recently, and the market's leverage level is not high."
    },
    {
      "zh": "通知同时要求证券公司加强管理，对交易不正常的投资者管理得更严格。同一天，深圳证券交易所还公布了一份规则草案，打算在创业板使用做市商制度；上海和深圳两家交易所也宣布减免多项费用，这一批一共超过27亿元。",
      "en": "The notice also asks securities companies to strengthen their management and to be stricter with investors whose trading is abnormal. On the same day, the Shenzhen Stock Exchange also published a draft set of rules, planning to use a market-maker system on the ChiNext board; the Shanghai and Shenzhen exchanges also announced cuts and waivers of many fees, worth more than 2.7 billion yuan in total in this batch."
    }
  ],
